<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="tw-section-white">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="text-center mb-5 tw-fade">
      <span class="tw-section-label">Frequently Asked Questions</span>
      <h2>Things people <em style="color:var(--tw-gold);">often wonder</em></h2>
      <hr class="tw-divider">
      <p style="max-width:520px;margin:1.25rem auto 0;">Here are answers to the questions Shimul hears most often from people considering therapy for the first time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="row g-4 tw-fade">
      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4"><div class="tw-faq-card"><h4 style="color:var(--tw-forest);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Does OHIP cover psychotherapy in Ontario?</h4><p style="color:var(--tw-text-mid);font-size:0.88rem;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">OHIP does not cover private psychotherapy. However, many extended health benefit plans and Employee Assistance Programs cover Registered Psychotherapists. Check with your provider before your first session. Shimul provides properly formatted receipts for insurance submission.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4"><div class="tw-faq-card"><h4 style="color:var(--tw-forest);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How often should I attend therapy?</h4><p style="color:var(--tw-text-mid);font-size:0.88rem;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">Most clients begin with weekly or bi-weekly sessions and adjust from there based on their needs and progress. Shimul works with you collaboratively to find a rhythm that genuinely supports your healing without feeling overwhelming.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4"><div class="tw-faq-card"><h4 style="color:var(--tw-forest);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Do you work with teenagers?</h4><p style="color:var(--tw-text-mid);font-size:0.88rem;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">Shimul currently works with adults aged 18 and older. If you are looking for support for a younger person, she will do her best to point you toward an appropriate referral in the Mississauga or Markham area.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4"><div class="tw-faq-card"><h4 style="color:var(--tw-forest);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Is everything I share completely confidential?</h4><p style="color:var(--tw-text-mid);font-size:0.88rem;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">Yes. Shimul is bound by CRPO ethical guidelines and Ontario privacy law. The only exceptions involve imminent risk of harm to yourself or others, or a court order. These are clearly explained in your intake documents before your first session.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4"><div class="tw-faq-card"><h4 style="color:var(--tw-forest);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What if I have never been to therapy before?</h4><p style="color:var(--tw-text-mid);font-size:0.88rem;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">Many of Shimul's clients come to Twish having never spoken to a therapist before. The free 15-minute consultation exists precisely for this: to ease you in gently, answer your questions, and let you get a feel for the process with no pressure or commitment.</p></div></div>
      <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4"><div class="tw-faq-card"><h4 style="color:var(--tw-forest);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How do I know if Shimul is the right fit?</h4><p style="color:var(--tw-text-mid);font-size:0.88rem;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">The therapeutic relationship matters enormously. Shimul encourages you to trust your instincts. If after your free consultation it does not feel like the right fit, she will help you find someone who is. The goal is always your wellbeing.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

